1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,460
But MIRI also presents a unique challenge.

2
00:00:03,910 --> 00:00:05,010
Webb has to stay cold.

3
00:00:05,670 --> 00:00:07,570
Otherwise, heat from the Sun and Earth

4
00:00:07,570 --> 00:00:10,010
would interfere with its night-vision-goggle view.

5
00:00:11,080 --> 00:00:14,300
So Webb has a huge sunshield that blocks the Sun's

6
00:00:14,300 --> 00:00:17,120
radiation, keeping the telescope extra cold.

7
00:00:18,720 --> 00:00:21,740
MIRI needs to stay even colder than the rest of the telescope.

8
00:00:22,580 --> 00:00:26,080
So onboard Webb, MIRI has its own special refrigerator,

9
00:00:26,280 --> 00:00:29,040
called the cryocooler, which uses helium

10
00:00:29,040 --> 00:00:33,640
to maintain a temperature below minus-440 degrees Fahrenheit,

11
00:00:34,400 --> 00:00:37,220
hovering just a few degrees above absolute zero.

